>
  <p>A general contractor in Anaheim handed me a stack of drawings dated 1987. He wanted to know if they were still right. The short answer: no. The slightly longer answer is what this guide is about, what an as-built drawing actually is, what should be in one, and why the original construction set sitting in his project file had become nearly useless after four decades of tenant fit-outs.</p>

